# Requisicoes prontas para o cofre-de-notas.
#
# Use com a extensao "REST Client" do VS Code, com o IntelliJ HTTP Client,
# ou copie os comandos curl equivalentes do README.

@base = http://localhost:3000
@email = ana@exemplo.com
@senha = uma-senha-longa-2026

### 0. saude do servico
GET {{base}}/saude

### 1. chave publica — e assim que qualquer outro servico verifica nossos tokens
GET {{base}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### 2. registrar
POST {{base}}/auth/registrar
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "senha": "{{senha}}" }

### 3. login — guarda o access token na variavel
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "senha": "{{senha}}" }

@access = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}

### 4. rota protegida SEM token -> 401 + WWW-Authenticate
GET {{base}}/notas

### 5. rota protegida COM token
GET {{base}}/notas
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### 6. criar nota
POST {{base}}/notas
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "texto": "comprar pao" }

### 7. ver o conteudo do token (SEM verificar) — so didatico
POST {{base}}/debug/decodificar
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{access}}" }

### 8. renovar — devolve access novo E refresh novo (rotacao)
# @name renovar
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}" }

### 9. REUSO: mandar de novo o refresh antigo -> queima a familia inteira
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}" }

### 10. rota de admin com usuario comum -> 403
GET {{base}}/admin/sessoes
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}

### 11. logout — mata access (jti) e refresh
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}" }

### 12. o access token de antes ja nao vale mais
GET {{base}}/notas
Authorization: Bearer {{access}}
